{"name":"Fruit Bowl","hex":"#fdc9d0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fruit bowl","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bowl used to keep fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fruit_bowl"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fruit Bowl","blocks":[{"text":"The Fruit Bowl was a postseason college football bowl game held in December at Kezar Stadium in San Francisco. The game was held three times, from 1947 to 1949. The first two games featured college teams and the last involved club teams."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit_Bowl","wikidata":"Q39086381"},{"title":"Fruit","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a fruit is the seed-bearing structure in flowering plants (angiosperms) that is formed from the ovary after flowering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg/330px-Fruit_Platter-_Seasonal_Fruits.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fruit","wikidata":"Q3314483"},{"title":"Bowl","blocks":[{"text":"A bowl is a typically round dish or container generally used for preparing, serving, storing, or consuming food. The interior of a bowl is characteristically shaped like a spherical cap, with the edges and the bottom, forming a seamless curve. This makes bowls especially suited for holding liquids and loose food, as the contents of the bowl are naturally concentrated in its center by the force of gravity. The exterior of a bowl is typically round but may vary in shape, including rectangular designs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/China%2C_Jiangxi_province%2C_Jingdezhen%2C_Ming_dynasty_%281368-1644%29%2C_Xuande_mark_-_Bowl_with_Decoration_of_the_%22Three_Friends%22_-_1953.631_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-330px-thumbnail.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bowl","wikidat